Commit:     Viche Recovery Steward <recovery-steward@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 19:25:09 2026 +0000

    Make unsafe-hold archiving safe under crash, retry and concurrency
    
    Address the final review conditions:
    
    * Serialize the entire read-archive-rewrite sequence with a mkdir lock whose
      pid file distinguishes a live holder from a crashed one. A live lock is
      respected; a dead-holder lock is stolen. The wait is bounded.
    * Create a missing archive atomically (hard link, temp+mv fallback) and treat
      an empty leftover archive as absent instead of letting an empty first file
      make the dedupe treat every extracted line as already archived.
    * Use FILENAME==ARGV[1] rather than NR==FNR for the dedupe, so an empty
      archive cannot swallow the extraction.
    * Remove non-POSIX find -maxdepth/-mmin stale-lock detection.
    * Tests now cover post-append interruption without duplication, an empty
      archive, a dead-holder lock being stolen, and a live-holder lock being
      respected and left intact.
    
    Focused test passes; full suite passes except the known protected
    ballot-integrity blocker.

